            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", guarantees the existence and uniqueness of the weak solution. This property ensures that the bilinear form is positive definite, which is a critical requirement for the finite element method. The weak formulation, represented by the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "inline_math",
              "expression": "B(u, v) = \\langle f, v \\rangle"
