            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Céa's Lemma is a fundamental result in the analysis of the finite element method (FEM) for elliptic partial differential equations. It provides a framework for proving error estimates by relating the exact solution of a variational problem to its finite-dimensional approximation. The lemma relies on the properties of Hilbert spaces, bilinear forms, and bounded linear operators. Specifically, it requires the bilinear form to satisfy continuity "
