              "type": "citation_occurrence",
              "occurrence_id": "221b6224-0d77-5a92-bfac-35567cf38cd8",
              "source_id": "wiki_c_a_s_lemma"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ".\n\nThe weak formulation of a partial differential equation is a critical component in the finite element method, enabling the use of variational principles and ensuring compatibility with numerical discretization. The weak form is typically expressed as a bilinear equation involving a bilinear form "
            },
            {
