              "expression": "|a(v, w)| \\leq \\gamma \\|v\\| \\|w\\|"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", where "
            },
            {
              "type": "inline_math",
              "expression": "\\gamma"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is a positive constant, and the coercivity of "
            },
            {
              "type": "inline_math",
              "expression": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is enforced by the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "inline_math",
              "expression": "a(v, v) \\geq \\alpha \\|v\\|^2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", where "
            },
            {
              "type": "inline_math",
              "expression": "\\alpha"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is also a positive constant. These properties, combined with the variational equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "inline_math",
              "expression": "a(u, v) = L(v)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", form the foundation for the analysis of the FEM.\n\nThe variational equation, "
            },
            {
              "type": "inline_math",
              "expression": "a(u, v) = L(v)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", represents the weak form of the partial differential equation, where "
            },
            {
              "type": "inline_math",
              "expression": "u"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is the solution in the Hilbert space "
            },
            {
              "type": "inline_math",
              "expression": "V"
            },
            {
