            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is a test function, and "
            },
            {
              "type": "inline_math",
              "expression": "L(v)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is a bounded linear functional. This equation forms the basis for the finite element discretization. The coercivity of the bilinear form, "
            },
            {
              "type": "inline_math",
              "expression": "a(v, v) \\geq \\alpha \\|v\\|^2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", guarantees the existence and uniqueness of the solution to the variational problem, as demonstrated by Céa's Lemma, a fundamental result in the analysis of the finite element method (FEM) for elliptic partial differential equations "
            },
            {
              "type": "citation_occurrence",
